/**
 * @file LumexHazardPointer
 * @brief Hazard pointer module: `hazard_pointer`, `hazard_pointer_obj_base`
 * and `make_hazard_pointer`, the interface of the C++26 `<hazard_pointer>`
 * from C++11 on.
 * @details Link <tt>%lumex::hazard_pointer</tt> (a compiled library; the
 * reader side is header-only). Works from C++11. A hazard pointer protects one
 * object that is read from an atomic pointer; a thread that removes the
 * object from the structure calls `retire` on it, and the object is deleted
 * only once no hazard pointer protects it. The classes follow [saferecl.hp]
 * of the C++26 draft (P2530R3) with the batch functions of P3428R4
 * (`make_hazard_pointer_batch`, `clear_hazard_pointer_batch`). The extension
 * `clean_up ()` runs a reclamation pass at once. One domain serves the whole
 * process; there are no custom domains, cohorts or executors, as in the
 * standard.
 *
 * The names are in `lumex::core::hazard_pointer`. The classes are the
 * module's own on every standard and toolchain (they are not aliases of the
 * C++26 standard ones, which no library ships yet); the API shape is the
 * standard's. The umbrella includes `base/LumexHazardPointerObjBase.hpp`,
 * `holder/LumexHazardPointerHolder.hpp` and
 * `holder/LumexHazardPointerBatch.hpp`; the engine (slots, retired lists,
 * reclamation) is in `engine/LumexHazardPointerEngine.hpp`.
 * @see The `README.md` page next to this umbrella (part of the documentation).
 */
#include "base/LumexHazardPointerObjBase.hpp"
#include "holder/LumexHazardPointerBatch.hpp"
#include "holder/LumexHazardPointerHolder.hpp"
